<title>UK: INTERVIEW - Yorkshire focus on polyester dyes.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - Yorkshire focus on polyester dyes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yorkshire Group Plc said on Monday that it had put its Australian pigments and inks business up for sale as part of a strategy of building on its world-leading position in polyester dyes.</p>
<p>In a telephone interview with Reuters, the group's new chief executive Stuart Wallis said that despite its small size, Yorkshire was &quot;very diverse in terms of geographic and product spread&quot; and lacked strategic direction.&quot;</p>
</text>
